    "task": {
      "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
      "params": {
        "text": "<h2>Build the Electron Configuration for Oxygen (O)</h2><p>Oxygen has 8 electrons. Drag the electrons (represented by arrows) into the correct orbital boxes following the Aufbau principle, Hund's rule, and the Pauli exclusion principle.</p><ul><li><strong>Aufbau principle:</strong> Fill orbitals from lowest to highest energy</li><li><strong>Hund's rule:</strong> Fill each orbital in a subshell with one electron before pairing</li><li><strong>Pauli exclusion principle:</strong> Maximum 2 electrons per orbital with opposite spins</li></ul><p><em>Order: 1s → 2s → 2p → 3s → 3p</em></p>"
      },
      "subContentId": "ad051467-73cf-4f44-9d17-6b8e39c1fc20",
